{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/africanfolder/posts/nigeria-leads-a-2026-global-extreme-poverty-ranking-with-an-estimated-731-millio/1105861925389646/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/africanfolder/posts/nigeria-leads-a-2026-global-extreme-poverty-ranking-with-an-estimated-731-millio/1105861925389646/","title":"African Folder","description":"Nigeria leads a 2026 global extreme poverty ranking with an estimated 73.1 million people affected, followed by DR Congo with 71.6 million. 🇳🇬🇨🇩\n\nAccording to figures attributed to World Data Lab,...","language":"en","text":"Nigeria leads a 2026 global extreme poverty ranking with an estimated 73.1 million people affected, followed by DR Congo with 71.6 million.\n\nAccording to figures attributed to World Data Lab, Afghanistan ranks third with 35.2 million people.\n\nSeven African countries appear in the top 10, showing the scale of poverty across the continent.\n\nThe ranking measures the number of people living in extreme poverty, not the percentage of each country's population.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n585 comments\n\n202 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nMagdeline Moloisane\n\nBoth countries are so rich. If they find a leader like Ibrahim Traore, it wouldn't take much to change the situation in both countries. The only thing they need are good leaders not thieves, infact the whole of Africa needs good leaders like Traore.\n\n43\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nZee Ntiny\n\nBut but but we have Dangote\n\n61\n\nView all 3 replies\n\nOnye Obodo\n\nPls say the Nothern part of Nigeria that’s what Islam gave to them\n\n24\n\nView all 11 replies\n\nView 1 reply\n\nBrian Mlambo\n\nI bet Nigerians are searching for south Africa we not on it\n\n15\n\nView 1 reply\n\nNeo M Mogoshi\n\nSo giants are hungry and starvin￼￼g\n\n5\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nLonda Gumede\n\nWe were once in this list. We thank our government for taking us out of this.\n\n7\n\nView 1 reply\n\nSizwe Mike Sibanyoni\n\nAs SOUTH Africans we shouldn't be laughing.. We should be keeping to. Ourselves because we were raised better than making fun of people who have nothing . Though, fight anyone and anything trying to stand between you and your country.\n\nI wish Africa saw its true potential\n\n3","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2137.1790379926097,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}